nit: More to the point?
```suggestion
    // The state is shared between the test, the request handler and the mock
    // socket. It is static since SocketTestingSetup::ConnectClient<T>() doesn't
    // allow for additional socket ctor args.
```

nit: Could skip explicit initialization since `std::atomic`-ctor implicitly initializes to `T()`[^1]/`false`[^2] and we overwrite the values immediately below anyway.

```suggestion
    static std::atomic_bool second_request_dispatched;
    static std::atomic_bool io_thread_in_send;
    static std::atomic_bool allow_second_reply;
```

[^1]: https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/atomic/atomic/atomic
[^2]: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3308028/default-constructor-value-for-bool-type

